of guest stars, and they tell stories about how you remembered them.
他们都会讲起你是如何记住他们的故事。

911
00:39:22.780 --> 00:39:27.960
I mean, I told a story today about how for five years you kept calling me in and we got
我是说，我今天还讲了一个故事，说你连续五年一直叫我去试镜，

912
00:39:27.960 --> 00:39:29.180
fan mail about it.
我们还因此收到过粉丝来信。

913
00:39:30.100 --> 00:39:30.920
Isabel H.
来自加利福尼亚州圣路易斯奥比斯波的伊莎贝尔·H.

914
00:39:31.120 --> 00:39:33.480
from San Luis Obispo, California, said,
说道，

915
00:39:34.340 --> 00:39:38.500
A lot of cast members have mentioned how you remember auditions and think of them for
很多演员都提到过你是如何记住试镜表现，并为他们考虑

916
00:39:38.500 --> 00:39:39.220
future roles.
未来的角色。

917
00:39:39.220 --> 00:39:43.640
It's a testament to how special you make actors feel and how much you remember them.
这证明了你让演员们感到自己有多特别，以及你对他们的记忆有多深刻。

918
00:39:43.640 --> 00:39:44.600
It's so touching.
这太感人了。

919
00:39:45.200 --> 00:39:49.700
How do you store all this information and have this kind of recall?
你是如何储存所有这些信息并拥有这种记忆力的？

920
00:39:50.240 --> 00:39:55.200
And then Caitlin from Syracuse, New York, said, Please talk about either your seemingly
还有来自纽约州锡拉丘兹的凯特琳说，请谈谈你那看似

921
00:39:55.200 --> 00:39:58.900
photographic memory or your amazing filing system.
照相般的记忆力，或者你那惊人的归档系统。

922
00:39:59.200 --> 00:40:03.480
So many times we have heard actors or guest actors talked about how you remembered them
我们听过太多次演员或客串演员谈论你是如何记住他们，

923
00:40:03.480 --> 00:40:05.940
and called them up for a role when it was right for them.
并在有适合他们的角色时打电话给他们。

924
00:40:06.200 --> 00:40:09.780
How on earth do you keep track of so many people?
你到底是怎么记住这么多人的？

925
00:40:11.320 --> 00:40:13.900
Well, in those days, we actually had memories.
嗯，在那个年代，我们确实有记忆力。

926
00:40:14.900 --> 00:40:17.220
We had an actual memory, not a digital memory.
我们有真正的记忆，而不是数字化的记忆。

927
00:40:17.640 --> 00:40:22.300
For me and for I will again speak for all my colleagues in casting, if we meet somebody
对我来说，我也可以代表所有选角同事说，如果我们遇到一个

928
00:40:22.300 --> 00:40:26.580
that we think is special or gives a good audition, you cannot wait to bring them again to get
我们认为特别或者试镜表现出色的人，就会迫不及待地想再次邀请他们，

929
00:40:26.580 --> 00:40:27.040
them a part.
给他们一个角色。

930
00:40:27.280 --> 00:40:31.120
And sometimes that takes 40 auditions before they get something.
有时这需要试镜40次，他们才能得到一个机会。

931
00:40:31.280 --> 00:40:33.440
And you have to just keep bringing them in and bringing them in.
你必须不断地邀请他们来试镜。

932
00:40:33.660 --> 00:40:37.700
But the memory part comes to probably me being old when my brain worked.
但记忆力那部分可能源于我大脑还好用的时候。

933
00:40:38.940 --> 00:40:43.100
And you do remember, because it's what we do, we do remember somebody who gives a great
你确实会记住，因为这就是我们的工作，我们会记住那些试镜表现出色的人，或者偶然遇到的人，然后说，哦，很高兴遇到他。

934
00:40:43.100 --> 00:40:46.220
audition or somebody you bump into and say, Oh, I'm glad I bumped into him.
我得让他来试这个角色，得让他来试那个角色。

935
00:40:46.360 --> 00:40:48.360
I got to bring him in for this, got to bring him from that role.
我认为这是选角工作中很重要的一部分，因为让你喜欢选角的原因，以及

936
00:40:48.480 --> 00:40:53.860
And that's a big part of casting, I think, because what makes you like casting and what
让我喜欢选角的原因，就是为合适的角色找到合适的人选。

937
00:40:53.860 --> 00:40:58.620
makes me like casting is getting the right person for the right role.
记住这些人的能力来自于面试了太多人。

938
00:40:59.760 --> 00:41:03.000
The remembering part comes from auditioning so many people.
当然，我会写下一些东西，记住他适合演脾气暴躁的人，或者记住

939
00:41:03.420 --> 00:41:08.000
And certainly I would write down something, remember him for somebody who's grumpy or remember
因为这家伙很棒，诸如此类的事情。

940
00:41:08.000 --> 00:41:10.000
because this guy was great, this, that, and the other thing.
然后你就会不断地邀请人们来试镜。

941
00:41:11.240 --> 00:41:13.100
And then you just keep bringing people in.
所以所有的选角导演都会这样做。

942
00:41:13.320 --> 00:41:14.600
So all the casting people do that.
我们只是看到了我们喜欢的人，就迫不及待地想给他们一份工作。

943
00:41:14.700 --> 00:41:17.340
We just see someone we love and we can't wait to get them a job.
而且，我们也会一直互相交流。

944
00:41:17.500 --> 00:41:19.340
And there's also, we talk with each other all the time.
我们会说，你一定要见见这个人。

945
00:41:19.460 --> 00:41:20.640
We're like, you got to meet this person.
这个人太棒了。

946
00:41:20.760 --> 00:41:21.860
This person was fabulous.
我们必须记住，因为那是我们工作的一部分。

947
00:41:22.560 --> 00:41:24.980
We just have to remember because that is part of our job.
而且，坦白说，30年前，你大脑本身的记忆力

948
00:41:24.980 --> 00:41:29.660
And also, again, frankly, 30 years ago, you did have a better memory in your own brain
确实比现在依靠数字设备要好。

949
00:41:29.660 --> 00:41:31.040
than you do now digitally.
我是说，我依然不是，我根本没有任何归档系统。

950
00:41:31.720 --> 00:41:35.120
I mean, I still am not, I have no filing system at all.
我根本没有任何归档系统。

951
00:41:35.480 --> 00:41:37.320
I look at my old audition sheets.
我会看我以前的试镜表。

952
00:41:37.500 --> 00:41:38.640
I look at my old auditions.
我会看我以前的试镜记录。

953
00:41:39.360 --> 00:41:44.100
If somebody is especially good, people I've met recently that I didn't know, wonderful
如果有人特别出色，比如我最近认识的一些新人，非常棒的

954
00:41:44.100 --> 00:41:45.380
standup name, Kat Cohen.
单口喜剧演员，凯特·科恩（Kat Cohen）。

955
00:41:45.600 --> 00:41:48.500
I can't wait to get her a really great, great job because she's so good.
我迫不及待想给她找一份非常非常好的工作，因为她太优秀了。

956
00:41:48.640 --> 00:41:50.100
And everybody I know will love her.
而且我认识的每个人都会喜欢她。

957
00:41:50.540 --> 00:41:51.620
Am I allowed to say that?
我能这么说吗？

958
00:41:51.660 --> 00:41:52.040
Yes.
可以。

959
00:41:52.360 --> 00:41:53.240
She'll be thrilled.
她会很高兴的。

960
00:41:53.460 --> 00:41:53.960
Yes, exactly.
没错，正是如此。

961
00:41:53.960 --> 00:41:56.160
She's pretty famous in the standup world.
她在单口喜剧界已经小有名气了。

962
00:41:56.380 --> 00:42:01.960
So when I see someone come along and I know that person is effing fabulous, I will not
所以当我看到有人出现，并且我知道那个人简直棒极了，我就不会

963
00:42:01.960 --> 00:42:03.940
stop until I get them something good.
停下来，直到为他们争取到好机会。

964
00:42:04.360 --> 00:42:08.360
And in my early days, the office early days, it was Kristen Schaal, people like that.
在我的早期，也就是办公室剧组的早期，有克里斯汀·沙尔（Kristen Schaal）那样的人。

965
00:42:08.480 --> 00:42:09.700
It was Jenna Fisher.
还有珍娜·费舍（Jenna Fischer）。

966
00:42:09.920 --> 00:42:11.600
It was just those people you had to work.
就是那些你必须与之合作的人。

967
00:42:11.780 --> 00:42:13.340
Neil Casey, all these unbelievers.
尼尔·凯西（Neil Casey），所有这些不可思议的人。

968
00:42:13.440 --> 00:42:13.900
Zach Woods.
扎克·伍兹（Zach Woods）。

969
00:42:14.380 --> 00:42:14.600
Yeah.
没错。

970
00:42:14.880 --> 00:42:15.220
Aubrey.
奥布瑞（Aubrey）。

971
00:42:15.740 --> 00:42:16.920
Just had to meet them.
就是必须得见见他们。

972
00:42:17.000 --> 00:42:18.500
And you're like, I got to get them in.
你会觉得，我得把他们引荐进来。

973
00:42:18.840 --> 00:42:19.660
Got to meet Mike Shore.
得去见见迈克·肖尔（Mike Shore）。

974
00:42:19.780 --> 00:42:20.780
Got to meet Greg Daniels.
得去见见格雷格·丹尼尔斯（Greg Daniels）。

975
00:42:20.920 --> 00:42:22.300
Because that is my job.
因为这就是我的工作。

976
00:42:22.300 --> 00:42:24.980
And it's also, thank God, what I like about it.
而且谢天谢地，这也是我喜欢这份工作的原因。

977
00:42:25.160 --> 00:42:31.320
So for whatever proclivity I have for actors and comedy people and people who make me laugh
所以，无论我对演员、喜剧人，以及那些能让我发笑的人有什么样的偏好，

978
00:42:31.320 --> 00:42:36.860
and people who are clearly very talented, maybe better at drama than comedy, blah, blah,
还有那些显然非常有才华的人，也许演正剧比演喜剧更好，诸如此类，

979
00:42:36.900 --> 00:42:37.140
blah, blah.
等等。

980
00:42:37.140 --> 00:42:40.880
We remember them because we like them and we can focus on that.
我们记得他们是因为我们喜欢他们，我们可以专注于这一点。

981
00:42:41.100 --> 00:42:44.840
You know, it's a whole discussion about how memory works.
你知道，这涉及到关于记忆如何运作的完整讨论。

982
00:42:45.020 --> 00:42:48.340
But still, I do not have any kind of digital anything now.
但即便如此，我现在没有任何数字化的东西。

983
00:42:48.480 --> 00:42:49.020
I don't watch.
我不看。

984
00:42:49.180 --> 00:42:52.460
I should, but I don't watch enough TikTok or YouTube or anything like that.
我应该看，但我看TikTok、YouTube或其他类似平台的时间不够多。

985
00:42:52.740 --> 00:42:54.740
I sort of remember visually as well.
我某种程度上也靠视觉记忆。

986
00:42:54.740 --> 00:42:55.860
I think I remember visually.
我想我是靠视觉记忆的。

987
00:42:56.080 --> 00:42:56.940
To get technical.
说得专业点的话。

988
00:42:57.280 --> 00:42:57.360
Yeah.
没错。

989
00:42:57.520 --> 00:42:57.740
Yeah.
没错。

990
00:42:57.840 --> 00:43:02.200
Do you also go to see Groundling shows or UCB shows?
你也会去看Groundlings或UCB的演出吗？

991
00:43:02.200 --> 00:43:02.520
Yes.
会。

992
00:43:02.520 --> 00:43:03.880
Not as much as I used to.
不像以前那么频繁了。

993
00:43:04.120 --> 00:43:05.460
Is that like a scouting thing?
那算是一种发掘人才的行为吗？

994
00:43:05.500 --> 00:43:10.120
I don't, I never per se went scouting, but I mean, as I'm here scouting or anything,
我不会，我从来没有专门去“发掘”过，我的意思是，我不是像在这里进行选角或类似的事情，

995
00:43:10.280 --> 00:43:12.020
like the poor agents have to do sometimes.
像那些可怜的经纪人有时不得不做的那样。

996
00:43:12.020 --> 00:43:15.700
They go to an industry night and they see if they should sign certain people or whatever.
他们去参加行业之夜，看看是否应该签下某些人什么的。

997
00:43:16.140 --> 00:43:22.060
We also have a network of comedy managers who need to get more credit than they ever get.
我们还有一个喜剧经纪人网络，他们理应得到比现在更多的认可。

998
00:43:22.360 --> 00:43:23.840
I didn't discover anybody.
我没有发掘任何人。

999
00:43:24.040 --> 00:43:27.620
The comedy manager discovered that person before I brought them in.
在带他们进来之前，是喜剧经纪人先发掘了他们。

1000
00:43:27.620 --> 00:43:30.480
You know, Christy Smith discovered Charlene Yee.
你知道，克里斯蒂·史密斯（Christy Smith）发掘了查琳·易（Charlene Yee）。

1001
00:43:30.600 --> 00:43:32.400
Jimmy Miller discovered everybody.
吉米·米勒发掘了所有人。

1002
00:43:32.660 --> 00:43:34.620
Dave Becky, Dave Miner.
戴夫·贝基，戴夫·迈纳。

1003
00:43:34.760 --> 00:43:39.740
They discovered all these people and brought them up from nothing and encouraged them and
他们发掘了所有这些人，让他们从无名小卒成长起来，鼓励他们，

1004
00:43:39.740 --> 00:43:41.640
put together these shows with them.
并与他们一起制作了这些节目。

1005
00:43:41.760 --> 00:43:45.160
And all the greats are with all these unbelievable comedy managers.
所有伟大的喜剧演员背后都有这些令人难以置信的喜剧经纪人。

1006
00:43:45.440 --> 00:43:47.820
So I give them all the credit for doing the discovering.
所以我把发掘人才的功劳都归于他们。

1007
00:43:48.120 --> 00:43:49.900
Well, that's how I feel about Naomi.
嗯，我对娜奥米也是这种感觉。

1008
00:43:50.220 --> 00:43:50.580
Naomi.
娜奥米。

1009
00:43:50.820 --> 00:43:51.140
I mean.
我是说。

1010
00:43:51.340 --> 00:43:53.720
Everybody she signs ends up on SNL.
她签下的每个人最后都上了《周六夜现场》。

1011
00:43:54.460 --> 00:43:54.860
Kristen Wiig.
克里斯汀·韦格。

1012
00:43:54.900 --> 00:43:55.220
It's amazing.
太神奇了。

1013
00:43:55.220 --> 00:43:56.060
Jerry Miner.
杰瑞·迈纳。

1014
00:43:56.140 --> 00:43:56.700
Yep, exactly.
没错，正是如此。

1015
00:43:56.700 --> 00:44:02.780
So for whatever reason, whatever thing we have in our brains that makes us focus on,
所以不管是什么原因，不管我们大脑中是什么东西让我们专注于此，

1016
00:44:02.920 --> 00:44:05.420
I mean, we can visually and hear people in our brains.
我是说，我们可以在脑海中想象人们的样子和声音。

1017
00:44:05.700 --> 00:44:06.800
Maybe we're all psychos.
也许我们都是疯子。

1018
00:44:06.880 --> 00:44:07.180
I don't know.
我不知道。

1019
00:44:08.860 --> 00:44:12.660
But whatever that is, comedy managers need to have a lot more credit too.
但无论那是什么，喜剧经纪人也应该得到更多的认可。

1020
00:44:12.820 --> 00:44:13.480
Do they get credit?
他们得到认可了吗？

1021
00:44:13.560 --> 00:44:14.020
I don't know.
我不知道。

1022
00:44:14.160 --> 00:44:14.780
I don't even know.
我甚至不知道。

1023
00:44:14.900 --> 00:44:16.540
But I always say I didn't discover a soul.
但我总是说我没发掘过任何人。

1024
00:44:16.680 --> 00:44:19.500
They all came from these great managers and agents.
他们都是来自这些伟大的经纪人和代理人。

1025
00:44:19.800 --> 00:44:24.100
And then slowly improv comedy kind of got a presence in the comedy world.
后来即兴喜剧在喜剧界慢慢有了一席之地。

1026
00:44:24.100 --> 00:44:26.100
And we would bring those people into audition.
我们会带这些人来试镜。

1027
00:44:26.740 --> 00:44:27.460
Let's see.
让我想想。

1028
00:44:27.580 --> 00:44:31.560
We have a question here from Kimberly Ness from Rochester, Minnesota.
我们这里有一个来自明尼苏达州罗切斯特市的金伯利·内斯的问题。

1029
00:44:31.920 --> 00:44:37.100
Writes in and says, Allison, what was your all-time favorite episode of The Office and why?
她写信问，艾莉森，你最喜欢《办公室》的哪一集？为什么？

1030
00:44:37.660 --> 00:44:38.180
Wow.
哇。

1031
00:44:40.000 --> 00:44:43.560
I mean, it could be as a fan or from a casting perspective, I guess.
我是说，我想这可以从粉丝的角度，或者从选角的角度来看。

1032
00:44:44.360 --> 00:44:47.960
Well, it would be both my all-time favorite episode.
嗯，这对我来说都是我最喜欢的一集。

1033
00:44:48.140 --> 00:44:56.360
It probably, as a fan, was the basketball one when Stanley was bouncing the basketball and he couldn't do it, that episode.
作为粉丝，我最喜欢的可能是斯坦利拍篮球的那一集，他当时拍不了球，就是那一集。

1034
00:44:56.360 --> 00:44:57.840
And I think I went to the set that day.
我想那天我去过片场。

1035
00:44:57.860 --> 00:44:58.980
So I saw a little bit of it.
所以我看了一点点。

1036
00:44:59.100 --> 00:44:59.620
So it was my favorite.
所以那是我的最爱。

1037
00:44:59.700 --> 00:45:01.700
That had to have been my all-time favorite episode.
那一定是我最喜欢的一集。

1038
00:45:01.860 --> 00:45:03.880
It's not everybody else's all-time favorite episode.
那可能不是其他人最喜欢的一集。

1039
00:45:04.000 --> 00:45:05.120
That's one of our all-time favorites.
那是我们最喜欢的一集。

1040
00:45:05.120 --> 00:45:05.500
Oh, it is?
哦，是吗？

1041
00:45:05.620 --> 00:45:06.920
That's a pretty great episode.
那确实是很棒的一集。

1042
00:45:07.120 --> 00:45:11.980
And also Phyllis' wedding for obvious reasons because it was Phyllis and she was so good.
还有菲利斯的婚礼，原因显而易见，因为那是菲利斯，她演得太好了。

1043
00:45:12.100 --> 00:45:14.680
And also Jim and Pam's wedding for sure.
当然还有吉姆和帕姆的婚礼。

1044
00:45:14.680 --> 00:45:18.060
And then you came dancing down the aisle like that YouTube video.
然后你们像那个YouTube视频里一样跳着舞走过过道。

1045
00:45:18.260 --> 00:45:19.940
I think they took that from the YouTube video.
我想他们是从那个YouTube视频里借鉴的。

1046
00:45:20.140 --> 00:45:20.260
They did.
确实是。

1047
00:45:20.540 --> 00:45:21.720
Yeah, so that was pretty cool.
是啊，那真的很酷。

1048
00:45:21.800 --> 00:45:23.780
I think those were my favorite episodes for sure.
我想那些绝对是我最喜欢的剧集。

1049
00:45:24.920 --> 00:45:33.660
Well, Allison, we just got so much mail for you because our fans just adore you and the work that you've done on creating The Office and so many of their favorite shows.
艾莉森，我们收到了很多寄给你的信，因为我们的粉丝非常崇拜你，也崇拜你在创作《办公室》以及他们喜爱的许多其他节目中所做的工作。

1050
00:45:33.680 --> 00:45:35.140
So I wanted to read you this.
所以我很想读给你听。

1051
00:45:35.460 --> 00:45:37.040
This is from Brenna C.
这是来自布伦娜·C的留言，

1052
00:45:37.220 --> 00:45:37.920
in New York.
坐标纽约。

1053
00:45:38.240 --> 00:45:39.000
Hi, Allison.
你好，艾莉森。

1054
00:45:39.200 --> 00:45:44.460
Not a question, but just wanted to say how much of an impact you have had on the television industry
这不是提问，我只是想说，多年来你对电视行业的影响有多么深远，

1055
00:45:44.460 --> 00:45:45.360
throughout the years.
贯穿了这些年。

1056
00:45:45.580 --> 00:45:53.120
It is so comforting and delightful to be watching a sitcom from a decade within the last 30 plus years and see your name pop up.
能看到过去三十多年里任何一部情景喜剧中出现你的名字，是一件非常令人欣慰和愉快的事。

1057
00:45:53.580 --> 00:46:00.960
You have been directly responsible for the most beloved characters on our screens, and that does not go unnoticed by fans.
你直接塑造了我们屏幕上最受喜爱的角色，粉丝们都看在眼里。

1058
00:46:01.140 --> 00:46:01.940
That's so nice.
太贴心了。

1059
00:46:02.180 --> 00:46:05.180
Anyone who knows TV knows Allison Jones.
任何了解电视行业的人都知道艾莉森·琼斯。

1060
00:46:05.620 --> 00:46:08.100
We see you and we appreciate you.
我们关注着你，也感激着你。

1061
00:46:08.100 --> 00:46:16.400
Thank you for taking chances on people who are trying to live their dreams because it makes dreams real for millions of people from that point on.
感谢你愿意给那些努力追梦的人机会，因为从那一刻起，这让数百万人的梦想成为了现实。

1062
00:46:16.940 --> 00:46:17.900
Thank you, Brenna.
谢谢你，布伦娜。

1063
00:46:18.360 --> 00:46:19.140
Isn't that so lovely?
这不是很可爱吗？

1064
00:46:19.140 --> 00:46:20.280
Yes, that's amazing.
是的，太棒了。

1065
00:46:20.520 --> 00:46:22.080
Yes, thank you so much.
是的，非常感谢。

1066
00:46:22.960 --> 00:46:23.440
Yes.
是的。

1067
00:46:23.620 --> 00:46:25.420
And we got a lot of letters like that.
我们收到了很多这样的信件。

1068
00:46:25.500 --> 00:46:26.140
That's incredible.
真是不可思议。

1069
00:46:26.140 --> 00:46:38.620
I mean, for me, Allison, I was out here for eight years, and you were the casting director that kept calling me back.
我是说，对我而言，艾莉森，我在这里待了八年，而你就是那位一直给我回电的选角导演。

1070
00:46:38.620 --> 00:46:44.960
I just needed you, really, to believe in me and give me that access to those parts.
我真的只需要你相信我，并给我接触那些角色的机会。

1071
00:46:45.220 --> 00:46:45.400
Right.
没错。

1072
00:46:45.400 --> 00:46:49.900
And that is what changed my life, but it also kept me going.
这不仅改变了我的生活，也让我坚持了下去。

1073
00:46:50.400 --> 00:46:57.280
I mean, just the fact that every six or seven months, Allison Jones would call with a part for me.
我的意思是，仅仅因为每隔六七个月，艾莉森·琼斯就会打来电话给我一个角色。

1074
00:46:57.520 --> 00:46:59.340
Maybe it was just a guest star.
也许只是个客串嘉宾。

1075
00:46:59.600 --> 00:47:00.900
Maybe it was a new pilot.
也许是一个新试播集。

1076
00:47:01.660 --> 00:47:05.580
That was why I wasn't flying back home to St. Louis and giving up.
这就是我没有飞回圣路易斯老家放弃的原因。

1077
00:47:05.700 --> 00:47:05.940
Yes, right, right.
是的，没错，没错。

1078
00:47:06.140 --> 00:47:09.520
Was because my phone would ring and you would bring me in.
就是因为我的电话会响，而你会叫我过去试镜。

1079
00:47:09.660 --> 00:47:09.980
Right.
没错。

1080
00:47:10.280 --> 00:47:12.020
And I so appreciate it.
我对此非常感激。

1081
00:47:12.020 --> 00:47:13.000
Oh, you're so welcome.
噢，不用客气。

1082
00:47:13.000 --> 00:47:16.880
And also, you're both so good at this, this podcast thing.
而且，你们俩都非常擅长做这个，这个播客节目。

1083
00:47:17.020 --> 00:47:17.780
It's quite amazing.
真是太神奇了。

1084
00:47:18.220 --> 00:47:18.960
Thank you.
谢谢。

1085
00:47:20.800 --> 00:47:26.800
But I would say that that is a large amount of faith that we have in people and in actors.
但我得说，我们对人们和演员有着极大的信任。

1086
00:47:26.980 --> 00:47:34.960
And when actors ask about what's the thing that you can advise actors on or what is the one word you have for actors, and I say tenacity.
当演员问我有什么建议，或者用一个词来形容演员时，我会说：坚韧。

1087
00:47:35.980 --> 00:47:38.280
Faith for the people who have to choose you.
对于那些必须做出选择的人来说，是信任。

1088
00:47:38.520 --> 00:47:41.580
Leap of faith for the people who have to choose you and for actors, tenacity.
对于那些必须做出选择的人来说，是孤注一掷的信任；而对于演员来说，是坚韧。

1089
00:47:42.260 --> 00:47:43.460
So many actors.
有太多的演员了。

1090
00:47:44.240 --> 00:47:45.200
God bless him.
上帝保佑他。

1091
00:47:45.300 --> 00:47:45.700
Ken Jeong.
肯·郑。

1092
00:47:46.000 --> 00:47:48.460
I brought him in so many times for Curb.
我曾多次让他来试镜《抑制热情》。

1093
00:47:48.680 --> 00:47:50.180
He finally got a Curb.
他最终得到了一个《抑制热情》的角色。

1094
00:47:50.320 --> 00:47:51.440
He finally got an office.
他最终得到了一个办公室的角色。

1095
00:47:52.080 --> 00:47:53.960
And now Ken is doing okay.
现在肯过得还不错。

1096
00:47:54.740 --> 00:47:58.580
But yes, we have faith and you have to have the tenacity.
但确实，我们有信任，而你们必须有坚韧。

1097
00:47:59.720 --> 00:48:05.920
So, and that is the big story of many successful actors, I think, having the tenacity and the –
所以，我认为这就是许多成功演员的大故事，拥有坚韧和——

1098
00:48:06.540 --> 00:48:12.440
My acting coach, he used to say, success is opportunity meets readiness.
我的表演教练曾说，成功是机会与准备的相遇。

1099
00:48:12.720 --> 00:48:12.980
Yes.
是的。

1100
00:48:13.180 --> 00:48:13.420
Yes.
是的。

1101
00:48:13.420 --> 00:48:15.200
You can't control the opportunities.
你无法掌控机遇。

1102
00:48:15.420 --> 00:48:15.580
Right.
没错。

1103
00:48:15.820 --> 00:48:17.320
But you can control the readiness.
但你可以掌控准备工作。

1104
00:48:17.620 --> 00:48:17.760
Right.
没错。

1105
00:48:17.980 --> 00:48:22.220
So you just be ready for when Allison Jones calls, basically.
所以你只需要做好准备，等待艾莉森·琼斯打电话来就行了。

1106
00:48:22.560 --> 00:48:23.900
You're the opportunity piece.
你就是那个机遇的关键。

1107
00:48:24.100 --> 00:48:24.440
Oh, good.
噢，太好了。

1108
00:48:24.520 --> 00:48:25.420
Thank you very much.
非常感谢。

1109
00:48:25.420 --> 00:48:30.140
And, you know, I just tried to always be ready.
而且，你知道，我一直努力让自己随时准备好。

1110
00:48:30.360 --> 00:48:35.320
And he also said the key is building a consistent body of work.
他还说，关键在于建立持续稳定的作品积累。

1111
00:48:35.380 --> 00:48:35.620
Yes.
是的。

1112
00:48:35.800 --> 00:48:41.080
So that every time – and he would literally use your name because you were the casting director that was calling.
这样每次——他甚至会直接提到你的名字，因为你就是那位打电话的选角导演。

1113
00:48:41.240 --> 00:48:47.780
He would say every time Allison calls, you are ready and you show her a consistent body of work.
他说每次艾莉森打电话来，你都要准备好，并向她展示你持续稳定的作品积累。

1114
00:48:47.780 --> 00:48:54.100
And if you do those two things, eventually, eventually, the right fit will find you.
如果你能做到这两点，最终，终有一天，最适合你的角色会找到你。

1115
00:48:54.480 --> 00:49:03.040
My first boss to whom I owe everything, the late Judith Wiener – anyway, I owe her everything in terms of any kind of casting theory.
我第一位老板，已故的朱迪丝·维纳，我欠她一切——总之，我在选角理论方面的一切都归功于她。

1116
00:49:03.500 --> 00:49:07.220
But she used to always say there is one perfect part for every actor.
但她过去常说，每个演员都有一个完美契合的角色。

1117
00:49:07.560 --> 00:49:08.720
So – and I believe that.
所以——我相信这一点。

1118
00:49:08.960 --> 00:49:11.300
She said there is one perfect part for every actor.
她说每个演员都有一个完美契合的角色。

1119
00:49:11.440 --> 00:49:11.800
Well –
嗯——

1120
00:49:11.800 --> 00:49:12.920
And keep bringing them in.
并且要不断地让他们参与进来。

1121
00:49:13.100 --> 00:49:13.320
Yeah.
是啊。

1122
00:49:13.580 --> 00:49:15.500
Thank you for fighting for us because –
谢谢你为我们争取，因为——

1123
00:49:15.500 --> 00:49:16.020
Oh, please.
噢，别这样。

1124
00:49:16.240 --> 00:49:17.360
We know you did.
我们知道你做了。

1125
00:49:17.920 --> 00:49:18.280
Yeah.
是啊。

1126
00:49:18.500 --> 00:49:19.500
We do all the time.
我们一直都在做。

1127
00:49:19.600 --> 00:49:21.680
We know we wouldn't be here without you, Allison.
我们知道没有你，我们就不会有今天，艾莉森。

1128
00:49:21.920 --> 00:49:22.240
Truly.
真的。

1129
00:49:22.480 --> 00:49:24.060
It means so much to us.
这对我们意义重大。

1130
00:49:24.300 --> 00:49:24.620
Really.
真的。

1131
00:49:24.640 --> 00:49:24.840
Yeah.
是啊。

1132
00:49:24.960 --> 00:49:25.140
I'll get –
我会——

1133
00:49:25.140 --> 00:49:25.820
Thank you for this.
谢谢你做的一切。

1134
00:49:25.940 --> 00:49:26.220
Choked up.
哽咽了。

1135
00:49:26.400 --> 00:49:26.560
Yeah.
是啊。

1136
00:49:26.640 --> 00:49:27.340
No, I would too.
不，我也会的。

1137
00:49:27.460 --> 00:49:27.560
Yeah.
是啊。

1138
00:49:27.560 --> 00:49:28.500
You changed our lives.
你改变了我们的人生。

1139
00:49:29.380 --> 00:49:37.480
After I came back to the office after interviewing with Greg and everybody, I remember saying to Phyllis, the before times Phyllis, God, I hope I get this job.
在和格雷格他们面试完回到办公室后，我记得我对菲利斯说——那是以前的菲利斯——天哪，我真希望我能得到这份工作。

1140
00:49:37.580 --> 00:49:39.860
I think it would be one of the most important jobs I've ever had.
我觉得这会是我做过最重要的工作之一。

1141
00:49:39.960 --> 00:49:41.500
This is – this show is fantastic.
这是——这部剧太棒了。

1142
00:49:41.520 --> 00:49:43.000
It's the office, blah, blah, blah, blah, blah.
这就是《办公室》，诸如此类的。

1143
00:49:43.580 --> 00:49:47.020
And little did I know it was more important for Phyllis.
当时我哪知道，这对菲利斯来说更重要。

1144
00:49:49.460 --> 00:49:49.940
Yeah.
是啊。

1145
00:49:50.320 --> 00:49:54.160
Hugely life-changing and important for me, but at the time, who knew?
对我来说这极大地改变了人生，意义非凡，但在当时，谁能预料到呢？

1146
00:49:54.500 --> 00:49:54.660
Yeah.
是啊。

1147
00:49:54.820 --> 00:49:55.060
Yeah.
是啊。

1148
00:49:55.220 --> 00:49:55.820
Who knew?
谁能预料到呢？

1149
00:49:55.960 --> 00:49:56.160
Who knew?
谁能预料到呢？

1150
00:49:56.160 --> 00:49:58.100
It was really important for Phyllis.
这对菲利斯来说真的很重要。

1151
00:49:58.240 --> 00:49:59.020
So amazing.
太棒了。

1152
00:49:59.020 --> 00:50:01.360
And for the people who make Inside Out.
还有那些制作《头脑特工队》的人们。

1153
00:50:01.780 --> 00:50:02.060
Yeah.
没错。

1154
00:50:02.520 --> 00:50:03.860
How proud are we of Phyllis?
我们有多为菲利斯感到骄傲？

1155
00:50:03.960 --> 00:50:04.720
She's amazing.
她太棒了。

1156
00:50:04.860 --> 00:50:05.020
So amazing.
太棒了。

1157
00:50:05.020 --> 00:50:05.620
I was crying.
我当时都哭了。

1158
00:50:05.740 --> 00:50:06.720
Yeah, that you just said.
是啊，你刚才也说了。

1159
00:50:08.320 --> 00:50:09.140
Hi, Phyllis.
嗨，菲利斯。

1160
00:50:09.280 --> 00:50:10.380
So happy for Phyllis.
真为菲利斯感到高兴。

1161
00:50:10.520 --> 00:50:11.440
So happy for Phyllis.
真为菲利斯感到高兴。

1162
00:50:11.440 --> 00:50:14.980
Well, Allison, this was absolutely delightful.
艾莉森，这期节目真是太愉快了。

1163
00:50:15.480 --> 00:50:22.440
Is there any memory or anything that we have not touched on that you'd like to share with our listeners?
还有什么我们没聊到的记忆或者其他事情，你想和听众们分享吗？

1164
00:50:22.820 --> 00:50:24.760
I'm going to look through our questions one more time.
我再看一遍我们的问题。

1165
00:50:24.760 --> 00:50:25.780
Yes, I would like to share.
是的，我想分享一下。

1166
00:50:25.880 --> 00:50:27.420
You had a question there that you didn't ask.
你刚才有个问题没问。

1167
00:50:27.560 --> 00:50:27.840
Oh.
噢。

1168
00:50:27.960 --> 00:50:33.860
You had asked on the questions something about a special phone call.
你在问题里提到了一个特别的电话。

1169
00:50:34.220 --> 00:50:34.780
Oh, yes.
噢，对。

1170
00:50:34.800 --> 00:50:35.400
Here it is.
在这儿呢。

1171
00:50:35.420 --> 00:50:35.660
Read that.
读一下那个。

1172
00:50:35.700 --> 00:50:36.160
Oh, yeah, yeah.
噢，对，对。

1173
00:50:36.380 --> 00:50:36.720
Yes.
是的。

1174
00:50:37.140 --> 00:50:38.300
This was my question.
这是我的问题。

1175
00:50:38.500 --> 00:50:38.600
Yes.
没错。

1176
00:50:38.600 --> 00:50:39.460
This is from Jenna F.
这是来自洛杉矶的珍娜·F发来的。

1177
00:50:39.600 --> 00:50:40.120
in Los Angeles.
在洛杉矶。

1178
00:50:40.120 --> 00:50:41.300
Oh, Jenna F.
噢，珍娜·F。

1179
00:50:41.540 --> 00:50:42.000
writes in sometimes.
她有时会写信来。

1180
00:50:42.020 --> 00:50:42.540
Okay, Jenna.
好的，珍娜。

1181
00:50:42.800 --> 00:50:42.860
Yeah.
嗯。

1182
00:50:43.100 --> 00:50:43.200
Okay.
好的。

1183
00:50:43.380 --> 00:50:52.960
Jenna said, I'm sure it's great to call and tell someone that they got a role, but you have to make a dozen other calls to tell all the other people that they didn't get the role.
珍娜说，我肯定打电话告诉别人他们得到了角色感觉很棒，但你还得打十几个电话去告诉其他人他们没得到这个角色。

1184
00:50:53.240 --> 00:50:54.540
And what's that like?
那是什么感觉？

1185
00:50:55.760 --> 00:50:59.780
Telling the actors they got the roles is the job, but mostly the managers and the agents.
通知演员他们得到了角色是工作的一部分，但主要是通知经纪人和代理人。

1186
00:50:59.940 --> 00:51:04.800
So we have to call and tell the agents and the managers that their client did or didn't get the role.
所以我们得打电话告诉经纪人和代理人他们的客户是否得到了角色。

1187
00:51:05.660 --> 00:51:08.220
And the one I remember the most is you, Jenna Fisher.
我印象最深的一次是关于你，珍娜·费舍尔。

1188
00:51:08.720 --> 00:51:09.160
What?
什么？

1189
00:51:09.160 --> 00:51:10.140
And you got the office.
你得到了《办公室》的角色。

1190
00:51:10.340 --> 00:51:10.600
Okay.
好的。

1191
00:51:12.360 --> 00:51:20.100
I probably, the worst call was having to tell Bob Odenkirk he didn't get the office, but I was able to tell the people who got the office, they got the office.
我可能觉得最糟糕的电话是不得不告诉鲍勃·奥登科克他没得到《办公室》的角色，但我能告诉那些得到角色的人，他们成功了。

1192
00:51:20.200 --> 00:51:21.320
So I called up Michael Green.
所以我给迈克尔·格林打了电话。

1193
00:51:21.740 --> 00:51:23.120
That was my agent at the time.
那是我当时的经纪人。

1194
00:51:23.320 --> 00:51:24.680
Your agent at the time, Michael Green.
你当时的经纪人，迈克尔·格林。

1195
00:51:24.920 --> 00:51:28.100
And they always know what you're calling about right after a teSt.
他们总是在试镜后就知道你打电话是为了什么。

1196
00:51:28.600 --> 00:51:29.920
And I said, hi, Michael.
我说，嗨，迈克尔。

1197
00:51:30.980 --> 00:51:36.140
And the import of it hit me as much as it probably hit him and would have hit you.
那一刻的重要性对我来说，就像它对他，或者对你一样，冲击力十足。

1198
00:51:36.140 --> 00:51:42.200
I said, I am calling to tell you that Jenna Fisher got the office.
我说，我打电话是想告诉你，珍娜·费舍尔得到了《办公室》的角色。

1199
00:51:43.420 --> 00:51:44.860
It's exactly what I said.
我就是这么说的。

1200
00:51:44.960 --> 00:51:45.880
And there was silence.
然后是一阵沉默。

1201
00:51:46.020 --> 00:51:46.600
There was silence.
当时一片寂静。

1202
00:51:46.780 --> 00:51:48.600
I think he was probably crying a little bit.
我想他当时可能有点想哭。

1203
00:51:48.860 --> 00:51:50.320
I was even getting emotional.
连我都有些感触。

1204
00:51:51.720 --> 00:51:59.640
Because for some reason at the time, it hit me that that was a big deal for Jenna Fisher to get the office.
因为不知为何，那一刻我突然意识到，能出演《办公室》对珍娜·费舍来说意义重大。

1205
00:51:59.840 --> 00:52:01.140
It was a big deal for me.
对我而言也意义重大。

1206
00:52:01.140 --> 00:52:04.100
And who even knew at the time what would happen with the office?
而且当时谁能预料到《办公室》后来会怎样呢？

1207
00:52:04.260 --> 00:52:04.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1208
00:52:04.760 --> 00:52:05.000
You know.
你知道的。

1209
00:52:05.680 --> 00:52:07.760
So that is the one that I remember the moSt.
所以那是我印象最深的一次。

1210
00:52:07.840 --> 00:52:09.220
I hate having to call.
我讨厌打电话。

1211
00:52:09.340 --> 00:52:10.300
I hate making those calls.
我讨厌打那种电话。

1212
00:52:10.540 --> 00:52:11.820
It falls on us, of course.
当然，这事儿得落到我们头上。

1213
00:52:11.960 --> 00:52:12.360
God forbid.
天哪。

1214
00:52:12.680 --> 00:52:15.760
Over the years, I've had to call and actually fire actors from a set.
这些年来，我不得不亲自打电话去剧组解雇演员。

1215
00:52:15.920 --> 00:52:16.540
It's awful.
那感觉糟透了。

1216
00:52:16.640 --> 00:52:17.300
No, it's awful.
不，那真的很糟糕。

1217
00:52:18.280 --> 00:52:20.600
Because people don't man up and do it themselves.
因为有些人不敢承担责任，不愿亲自去做。

1218
00:52:20.860 --> 00:52:21.880
You know, directors and things.
你知道，比如导演之类的人。

1219
00:52:21.980 --> 00:52:23.020
They don't want to do that kind of thing.
他们不想做那种事。

1220
00:52:23.080 --> 00:52:24.280
So we get to do the dirty work.
所以脏活累活就得我们来干。

1221
00:52:24.880 --> 00:52:34.960
So what it's like is it's awful, but it's great to be able to tell an agent or a manager that their client got a huge role that we know will be life-changing.
这种感觉很复杂，虽然解雇人很糟糕，但能告诉经纪人或经理他们的客户得到了一个我们深知会改变其一生的重要角色，那种感觉又棒极了。

1222
00:52:35.540 --> 00:52:39.320
And even the best are the small roles that will be life-changing.
即便是那些小角色，也同样能改变人生。

1223
00:52:39.440 --> 00:52:47.680
When I get to hire somebody phenomenal for one line on Curb Your Enthusiasm, and they're the ones who send bottles of wine and flowers.
当我能为《抑制热情》雇佣一个只演一句台词的非凡演员时，他们往往会送来红酒和鲜花。

1224
00:52:47.920 --> 00:52:50.860
It's like, yeah, you're spending your whole salary and it's one line.
就好像，没错，你把整份薪水都花掉了，而那只是一句台词。

1225
00:52:50.980 --> 00:52:53.100
But to them, it's the start of everything.
但对他们来说，那是这一切的开端。

1226
00:52:53.100 --> 00:52:59.420
So that's what's the greatest part of casting is getting these people you believe in, finally getting them the gigs.
所以选角最棒的部分，就是让你看好的人终于得到了工作机会。

1227
00:52:59.960 --> 00:53:01.860
And it takes so long.
而且这需要很长的时间。

1228
00:53:02.300 --> 00:53:04.760
Jack Black used to come in for one-line parts all the time.
杰克·布莱克过去常常来试镜那些只有一句台词的角色。

1229
00:53:04.800 --> 00:53:05.920
And he killed it.
而且他表现得非常出色。

1230
00:53:06.120 --> 00:53:08.380
And talk about a person who could kill one line.
说到能把一句台词演得精彩绝伦的人。

1231
00:53:08.480 --> 00:53:09.060
It was Jack Black.
那绝对是杰克·布莱克。

1232
00:53:09.360 --> 00:53:10.500
I could kill in a good way.
我是说那种好的意义上的精彩。

1233
00:53:11.200 --> 00:53:14.200
And when he finally started getting the parts, it was phenomenal.
当他终于开始接到角色时，那真是太惊人了。

1234
00:53:14.600 --> 00:53:18.740
You know, the rest is history for Jack Black, but still probably a full decade of Jack Black.
你知道，杰克·布莱克后来的成就众所周知，但他确实经历了整整十年的磨砺。

1235
00:53:18.880 --> 00:53:21.640
But anyway, it's the small parts that are pretty amazing, too.
总之，那些小角色也同样令人惊叹。

1236
00:53:21.640 --> 00:53:23.300
And the unknown people to get a part.
还有那些默默无闻的人获得角色时。

1237
00:53:23.500 --> 00:53:26.260
You know that it's a joyful, wonderful thing.
你知道那是一件多么令人愉悦、美妙的事情。

1238
00:53:26.640 --> 00:53:27.680
Allison, this was amazing.
艾莉森，这太棒了。

1239
00:53:27.960 --> 00:53:29.860
Thank you so much for coming in.
非常感谢你今天能来。

1240
00:53:30.100 --> 00:53:31.780
Yes, Allison, thank you.
是的，艾莉森，谢谢你。

1241
00:53:32.080 --> 00:53:36.220
You had such a deeply impactful role in casting The Office.
你在《办公室》的选角工作中发挥了极其深远的影响。

1242
00:53:36.520 --> 00:53:40.420
And I'm just so excited to share this interview with our fans.
我非常期待与我们的粉丝分享这次采访。

1243
00:53:44.390 --> 00:53:46.970
Well, I just loved that so much.
嗯，我真的很喜欢这次交流。

1244
00:53:47.310 --> 00:53:51.490
You know, Angela, I realize we never even cracked open her three pins of stuff.
你知道吗，安吉拉，我意识到我们甚至还没打开她那三个别针盒呢。

1245
00:53:51.750 --> 00:53:54.210
I know, but she said she'll bring them back any time.
我知道，但她说她随时都可以带回来。

1246
00:53:54.390 --> 00:53:56.830
We all laughed about it after we finished the interview.
采访结束后我们还一起拿这事儿开玩笑。

1247
00:53:57.050 --> 00:53:58.430
We were like, Allison.
我们当时说，艾莉森。

1248
00:53:58.790 --> 00:54:00.490
You carry those all the way up.
你竟然把那些东西全带上来了。

1249
00:54:00.650 --> 00:54:01.570
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

1250
00:54:02.150 --> 00:54:04.310
And I just love getting to see her in person.
我真的很喜欢能亲自见到她。

1251
00:54:04.530 --> 00:54:09.190
We've traded so many emails back and forth over the years of doing this podcaSt.
在做这个播客的这些年里，我们互通了太多的邮件。

1252
00:54:09.190 --> 00:54:13.870
And Angela, I know you ran into her recently, but I had not seen her in person in so long.
安吉拉，我知道你最近碰见过她，但我已经好久没见到她本人了。

1253
00:54:13.930 --> 00:54:14.850
And it was so great.
那感觉真是太棒了。

1254
00:54:15.070 --> 00:54:15.650
It was.
确实。

1255
00:54:15.750 --> 00:54:16.670
It was just so wonderful.
真是太美好了。

1256
00:54:17.210 --> 00:54:19.930
Well, thank you, everyone, for writing in with your questions.
那么，感谢大家写信发来你们的问题。

1257
00:54:19.930 --> 00:54:21.230
They were just terrific.
这些问题都太棒了。

1258
00:54:21.270 --> 00:54:23.790
And let us know who you want us to talk to next.
也请告诉我们你们接下来想让我们采访谁。

1259
00:54:24.050 --> 00:54:31.110
And don't forget, on Monday, we are going to start rerunning our rewatch, starting with the pilot.
别忘了，周一我们将开始重播我们的重温系列，从试播集开始。

1260
00:54:31.110 --> 00:54:35.130
And we have some really fun second drink tidbits for that one.
而且我们为那一集准备了一些非常有趣的“第二杯”花絮。

1261
00:54:35.250 --> 00:54:40.510
We're going to pop on before every episode and give you some new thoughts and observations about those episodes.
我们会在每一集开始前露面，分享我们对那些剧集的一些新想法和观察。

1262
00:54:40.730 --> 00:54:42.610
And some new nuggets that we're finding.
还有我们新发现的一些干货。

1263
00:54:42.970 --> 00:54:45.310
All right, you guys, we hope you had a great Wednesday.
好了，各位，希望你们度过了一个愉快的周三。

1264
00:54:45.310 --> 00:54:48.670
We will see you next week for more Office Ladies 6.0.
我们下周见，继续收听《办公室女士》6.0版。

1265
00:54:48.770 --> 00:54:49.310
See you then.
到时见。

1266
00:54:56.970 --> 00:54:58.910
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1267
